    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (80.18) and **Junior Caminero** (75.15), our two strongest plays. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a massive 0.479 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Englert, while **Junior Caminero** is buoyed by an ideal spot in the lineup and a high-ceiling matchup against Lambert. Both **Trea Turner** (74.00) and **Kyle Schwarber** (73.62) are prime targets against Avila, as the favorable 5.01 xERA of the opposing starter provides an excellent environment for both run production and power. We are particularly aggressive in exploiting the stolen base scarcity today; **Trea Turner**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Christian Yelich** all benefit from defensive speed factors\u2014specifically the slow deliveries of their respective matchups\u2014that keep their efficiency scores in the elite/strong tier despite varying baseline projections.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Luke Raley** on the bench. Despite his 57.71 score and a decent matchup against Yesavage, he fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace starters like **Lars Nootbaar** or **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. **Lars Nootbaar** ultimately secured the final outfield spot due to a +11% dynamic platoon edge and higher park factor. We are monitoring the lineup for **Caleb Durbin**, whose status remains \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have assumed a #5 spot, any drop in the order or a confirmed absence would necessitate a shift, as his current 66.15 score is heavily predicated on his expected placement. No major weather concerns have been flagged, but managers should keep a close eye on the catcher position; while **Gary Sanchez** (61.81) and **Dillon Dingler** (47.47) provide coverage, the latter faces a higher-skill matchup against Rocker, necessitating careful monitoring of the official lineups for any late-scratch risks.",
